# pi-extensions.conf — exact commands to install pi extensions/tooling
# inside the pi-agent container, run interactively (TTY attached) in the
# order listed, one `engine exec -it` invocation per line, so you can
# follow and answer any interactive prompts each command produces.
#
# Rules:
#   - One full shell command per line (it is passed to `bash -c "..."`).
#   - Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#   - Commands run with CWD=/root inside pi-agent, as root.
#   - Run `pi-ramalama --render-mounts` (or just `pi-ramalama --start`/`--setup`,
#     which call it) BEFORE `pi-ramalama --install-extensions`: mounts in
#     pi-mounts.conf must exist on the container before extensions write
#     into those paths, or the writes get shadowed when the mount is added
#     afterwards.
#   - Failure of one line does not stop the rest; failures are summarized
#     at the end.

# Example:
# pi extensions install @earendil-works/example-extension
# pi extensions list

